   "scion_answer": "$$\\frac{-5}{9} \\cdot \\frac{8}{17} = \\frac{-5 \\cdot 8}{9 \\cdot 17} = \\frac{-40}{153}$$\n\nThe numerator and denominator have no common factors (since $40 = 2^2 \\cdot 5$ and $153 = 3^2 \\cdot 17$), so the fraction is already in simplest form.\n\n$$\\boxed{\\frac{-40}{153}}$$",
