  {
   "id": "math-0013",
   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "To find the 2007th digit to the right of the decimal point in the decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$, we first determine the decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{7} = 0.142857142857142857\\ldots$$\n\nThe repeating part is **142857**, which has 6 digits. This means the pattern repeats every 6 digits.\n\nTo find the 2007th digit, we compute the remainder when 2007 is divided by 6:\n\n$$2007 \\div 6 = 334 \\text{ remainder } 5$$\n\nSo the 2007th digit corresponds to the **5th digit** in the repeating cycle 142857.\n\nThe digits of the repeating cycle are:\n$$1, 4, 2, 8, \\boxed{5}, 7$$\n\nTherefore, the 2007th digit to the right of the decimal point is $\\boxed{5}$.",
