   "id": "math-0020",
   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "To round $6287215$ to the nearest ten thousand:\n\n1. **Identify the ten thousands place:** In $6287215$, the digits are:\n   - Millions: 6\n   - Hundred thousands: 2\n   - **Ten thousands: 8**\n   - Thousands: 7\n   - Hundreds: 2\n   - Tens: 1\n   - Ones: 5\n\n2. **Look at the digit in the thousands place (the deciding digit):** The thousands digit is **7**.\n\n3. **Apply the rounding rule:** Since $7 \\geq 5$, we round **up**.\n\n4. **Round up:** Increase the ten thousands digit from 8 to 9, and set all digits to the right to zero:\n\n$$6287215 \\approx 6290000$$\n\nWe can also verify by checking which is closer:\n- $6287215 - 6280000 = 7215$\n- $6290000 - 6287215 = 2785$\n\nSince $2785 < 7215$, the number is closer to $6290000$.\n\n$$\\boxed{6290000}$$",
